	abstract = {—In the Software Development Life Cycle, modelling plays a most significant role in designing and developing software efficiently. Acceptance Test-Driven Development (ATDD) is a powerful agile software development model where a customer provides user acceptance test suits as a part of Software Requirements Specifications. A design has to develop a system so that User Acceptance Tests will be successful. In some systems, the Combinatorial Logic and Combinatorial Testing play a very crucial role. The authors have proposed a novel approach to enhance the existing Acceptance Test Driven Development model to Combinatorial Logic Oriented-ATDD model by incorporating combinatorial logic. Refinement with respect to combinatorial logic needs to be incorporated in all the stages of Software Development Life Cycle, i.e. starting from Software Requirement Specifications to User Acceptance Tests. This comprehensive approach derives the acceptance tests from user requirements effectively and efficiently. In this paper, the existing Indian Railway Reservation System is considered as a case study, and it was fully implemented as per proposed Combinatorial Logic Oriented-ATDD model. © 2020 Science and Information Organization. All rights reserved.},
