	affiliations = {Department of Computer Science, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi, Corpus Christi, TX, United States; Department of Computer Science, Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi, Corpus Christi, United States},
	abstract = {This research aims to evaluate the capabilities of Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) in automatically generating software development artifacts, such as project vision, project plan, software requirements specification, software design description, and software test description. The study compares manual artifact generation vs. ChatGPT's automated artifact generation. The research results indicate that ChatGPT can produce accurate, coherent artifacts with significantly reduced effort and time. While the efficiency achieved for software documentation generation utilizing ChatGPT is around 40%, the document quality achieved utilizing ChatGPT was a little lower than what is achieved with the manual approach. ChatGPT demonstrated usefulness across various development tasks, with some limitations, such as the need for human validation in some cases. The findings indicate that GenAI can enhance software documentation efficiency and productivity if integrated appropriately into development workflows. Further research is needed on ChatGPT's real-world applicability and comparison to other AI models. This study provides valuable insights into ChatGPT's potential as an automated software artifact generation tool. ©2025 IEEE.},
	author_keywords = {Automated Software Documentation; Generative AI; Generative AI for Software Engineering; Generative Artificial Intelligence; Software Documentation; Software Documentation Generation},
	keywords = {Artificial intelligence; Automatic test pattern generation; Efficiency; Information systems; Information use; Software design; Software testing; System program documentation; Automated software documentation; Effectiveness and efficiencies; Generative AI; Generative AI for software engineering; Generative artificial intelligence; Project vision; Software documentation; Software documentation generation; Automation},
