	abstract = {Maintaining consistency between models in development processes in different engineering disciplines is a challenging task. Though in software engineering exist many case tools which allow the editing of models and include code generators for reverse or round trip engineering, the source code is edited by specialized development environments. The same holds for other models, such as e.g., requirements specifications or technical design drawings in mechanical or chemical engineering or in architecture. The editing tools are often decoupled from each other. Additionally, modifications of the models are performed simultaneously. Tool support for maintaining consistency between models is urgently needed. In this paper, we present a research prototype for recovering structural consistency between software design and source code using a design tool and a development environment. The tool manages relationships between design model and source code and performs transformations based on declarative visual specifications of correspondence relations.},
