	abstract = {This paper proposes the efficient and adequate Computer Validation (CV) method for Pharmaceutical Automatic Control Software (PACS) using software components. CV is defined as "CV validates the PACS's soundness based on the documents related to the PACS and exhaustive test." Historically, PACS was newly developed in each development and the documents related to the design and test were newly developed in each development. For the pharmaceutical product manufactures, following tasks became grater workload: a) to develop documents related to the designs and tests, and b) to confirm the traceability between documents and functions of PACS. To reduce these workloads, we propose the CV method using software components. We carried out domain analysis. As the result of the analysis, we found out that the most functions that PACS has are similar. To use this characteristic, we developed software components and document templates before staring PACS developments. The software components and document templates were developed as the parameter customize type, and they can be customized by setting information of PACS without modification of codes and templates. Furthermore, we developed database that manages PACS information. To evaluate proposed method, we have applied proposed method to actual PACS development cases. As the result, we achieved following advantages, 1) to trace every requirement from requirement specification to test specifications seamlessly and to develop PACS that adapt to the requirement specification, and 2) to reduce working time of CV to 50[%].},
